== SUMMARY
Marek's rule as stated ("once kmax - k <= sets still missing, the new vertex must come from one of them")
loses tilings when sets overlap: 116 of 300 random overlapping trials lost some, 0 of 150 disjoint trials.
It counts sets, but one vertex type can belong to several sets, so fewer vertices than sets may finish the job.
The cover rule (prune when the fewest vertex types, from the root's index on, that could still meet every
missing set exceed the orbits left; plus a final check that every set is met) lost nothing in every case and
pruned harder: 21% of the unpruned nodes on overlapping sets, 4% on disjoint ones (Marek's: 30%, 14%).
Patch and scripts: experiments/required-sets-2026-10-26/.

